From c14a93f589d1d9fd1714a266c2afea7fed7772b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:21:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(ui): pick the GPU adapter by adapter, not only by
 backend, and log slow frames

Hybrid Intel UHD + NVIDIA laptops either landed on an adapter that never
rendered or refused outright; the old chain varied only the backend mask
and took wgpu's default-power adapter.

Changes:
- gpu_init.rs (new): per backend mask (preferred -> PRIMARY -> all),
  enumerate every adapter and log each (name, vendor, device, type,
  backend, presentable); try candidates one by one - request_device, a
  capability-driven surface config, and a configure checked inside a
  validation error scope + unwind guard. A failure logs its named reason
  and moves to the next adapter; adapters that failed under an earlier
  mask are not retried. When none works, the refusal names every adapter
  tried and why, on stderr and in a native dialog (no silent window).
- gpu_select.rs (new, pure): candidate order and surface config.
  Order: the --gpu/CAMCRAFT_GPU named adapter -> the GPU wgpu's
  PowerPreference::HighPerformance request answers with -> every other
  presentable adapter, discrete > integrated > virtual > other > cpu;
  ties go to the platform's native backend (DX12 on Windows, Metal on
  macOS, Vulkan elsewhere), then enumeration order. Unpresentable
  adapters are skipped by name.
  Config: the surface's own first format, Fifo unless absent, Opaque
  alpha when offered else the first reported mode (was get_default_config
  + a hard-wired AutoVsync).
- gpu.rs: `--gpu <name substring>` over `CAMCRAFT_GPU`, the same pattern
  as --gpu-backend / CAMCRAFT_GPU_BACKEND; a valueless flag refuses.
- frame_watch.rs (new) + shell draw: a frame over 100 ms is logged with
  its phases (commands+scene, ui, acquire, encode, submit+present),
  rate-limited to one line per 5 s.

Stall: not found headlessly. No blocking readback or device.poll(Wait)
is on the idle frame path (readbacks are tests/diagnostics only; the
traced-stock eye marches only with Deviate/playback armed). The leading
suspect is Vulkan-on-Optimus cross-adapter presentation, which the
native-backend-first order avoids on Windows; the frame-time log pins
the phase from the reporter's machine.

Tests: gpu_select::tests (discrete_before_integrated_before_cpu,
user_choice_wins_case_insensitively, unmatched_choice_is_said_and_auto_order_stands,
high_performance_pick_leads_on_its_best_backend,
unpresentable_adapters_are_skipped_by_name, nothing_to_order_is_empty_not_a_panic,
log_line_names_every_field, config_comes_from_reported_capabilities,
incompatible_surface_refuses_by_name), frame_watch::tests (3),
gpu::tests::adapter_choice_flag_then_env.

Refs #74

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
