From cd35ee1049a52dc030477de87a2f64ff6492d5b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:58:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(ui): check GPU bring-up for OOM, internal errors and
 device loss; try the next adapter on a View3D failure

PR #76 review fixes:
- configure, the View3D build and one presented test frame run inside
  Validation + OutOfMemory + Internal error scopes with a device-lost
  callback and a bounded poll; any failure names the adapter and the
  next one is tried (a lost device no longer passes as Ok)
- the same GPU across backends matches on PCI vendor + device ids when
  both are non-zero (name only otherwise), so DX12 keeps the HP rank
- the refusal lists skipped adapters and empty backend masks instead of
  "no GPU adapter was found"
- the View3D pipeline is built per candidate: a failure drops that
  adapter and tries the next instead of exiting with no dialog
- --gpu=x / --gpu-backend=x parse; a surface-handle failure keeps the
  failures collected so far; doc line on --gpu-backend narrowing --gpu
- tests: same_gpu_named_differently_per_backend_still_leads_on_dx12,
  refusal_names_tried_and_skipped_adapters, empty_alpha_modes_refuse_by_name,
  caps_without_render_attachment_refuse_by_name, equals_form_flags_are_parsed

Refs #74

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
